\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Note that we can assume without loss of generality that: (1) every edge in $S_n$ has exactly $k$-times on each edge and (2) that all times are multiples of $2$. This follows from the fact that we can construct from any $\starexp(k)$-instance $(S_{n'}, u)$ another $\starexp(k)$-instance $(S_n, \tau)$ so that : $(S_n, \tau)$ is explorable if and only if $(S_{n'}, u)$ also is and every time in $(S_n, \tau)$ satisfies conditions (1) and (2).
