The Track A version does not survive the paper’s own “what algorithm produces the certificate?” test on the proposed planted distribution: a standard colored branch-and-bound clique search recovers the planted witness quickly at moderate sizes. I’m therefore switching to an honest Track B family on the paper’s native temporal-star object. Its general mechanical route is bipartite matching; the compact route is a single modular invariant in the availability rows, and the answer remains an actual complete temporal exploration rather than a finite-field surrogate.
