/tmp/tmp.IgPwFcFsGj/main.tex:168:A \emph{temporal Eulerian circuit} in a temporal graph $(G, \tau)$ is a closed temporal walk $(e_1,t_1),\dots,(e_m,t_m)$ such that $e_1\ldots,e_m$ is an Euler circuit in the underlying static graph $G$. If there exists a temporal Eulerian circuit in $(G, \tau)$, then we call $(G, \tau)$ \emph{temporally Eulerian}.
