The successful Gemini answers expose the current construction completely: they are exact constant-step arithmetic progressions, so increasing only `n` mostly lengthens transcription and does not harden the insight. I’m replacing that visible progression with a certificate-preserving binary-linear change of variables. The witness remains a native temporal-star exploration, but its compact route becomes an XOR invariant recoverable in 281 operations at 256 leaves; the standard matcher remains the explicitly disclosed Track B algorithm.
