Implemented and locally verified a Track B temporal-star exploration generator based on the paper’s native `StarExp` problem. The paper establishes NP-completeness for `k ≥ 4` while identifying bounded interval-membership-width and evenly spaced times as tractable regimes. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.05387)

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2103.05387/gen_2103_05387.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2103.05387/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2103.05387/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2103.05387/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2103.05387/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2103.05387/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- G1–G9(c) pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- Hopcroft–Karp reference: 8/8, as expected for Track B.
- Answer: 1,170 characters, 256 atoms.
- Intended XOR-invariant route: 281 operations.
- Additional deterministic, detached-verifier, parser, and invariant checks passed on 400 instances.

The result is not yet shippable: all 12 required oracle retries received `HTTP 403: Key limit exceeded (total limit)`, so no Step 4 attempt was scored. Restoring the OpenRouter quota and rerunning `harden.py` is the only remaining blocker.
